# Trivy ignore file — CVEs accepted as no Debian package fix is available.
# These all have upstream patches, but the patched packages are not yet in
# the Debian stable apt repository, so apt-get upgrade cannot resolve them.
#
# Last reviewed: 2026-08-11. Rebuilt the image locally (linux/amd64, matching
# the GitHub Actions runner architecture that actually executes the CI Trivy
# scan) and ran `trivy image` against it fresh. Findings below were removed
# because they no longer reproduce; everything else was re-verified present.
#
# Two things learned during this review, worth knowing before editing this
# file again:
# 1. The base image (python:3.13-slim) is now on Debian 13 (Trixie), not
#    Debian 12 (Bookworm) as previously assumed — but most of the specific
#    CVE IDs below turned out to still apply (same long-unfixed upstream
#    issues persist release over release), so most of the list carried over.
# 2. `apt-get update`/`upgrade` pulls whatever the live Debian mirror serves
#    at build time, so an image built for linux/arm64 vs linux/amd64 (or at
#    a different moment) can land on a genuinely different package snapshot
#    with a different CVE set — a rebuild for arm64 during this review
#    surfaced ~90 additional, newer CVEs not present in the amd64 build.
#    This file is scoped to what the CI-published amd64 image actually
#    contains; it is not a perfectly stable pin. Re-verify by rebuilding
#    for linux/amd64 and running `trivy image` locally before trusting an
#    old review date.
#
# CI's Trivy step (reusable-docker-build.yml) runs with `ignore-unfixed: true`,
# so a CVE with no fix available never reaches code scanning, listed here or
# not. Its `severity: CRITICAL,HIGH` does not limit the SARIF upload: MEDIUM
# findings show up too (e.g. code-scanning alert #594). Everything in this file
# exists for the benefit of a broader manual `trivy image` scan (no
# --ignore-unfixed, all severities).
#
# 2026-10-07: removed the pip and setuptools/msgpack entries (CVE-2026-6357,
# CVE-2025-47273, CVE-2026-59890, GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964). Trivy read them from
# pip's pip/_vendor/vendor.txt, and the Dockerfile now uninstalls pip,
# setuptools and wheel from the runtime image. A linux/amd64 scan with no
# ignore file finds no Python-package CVEs at all.

# --- Debian base image system package CVEs — no fix available in Debian repos ---
# These affect system tools not invoked by this application at runtime. The container
# runs as a non-root user (uid 1000). All have no Debian backport at time of writing.
# None of these are CRITICAL/HIGH-with-a-fix, so CI's `ignore-unfixed` already
# excludes them from the actual gate — kept here for broader manual-scan hygiene.

# tar: does not warn about setuid/setgid files on extraction
# Risk: low — tar not invoked by this application at runtime
CVE-2005-2541

# login.defs/passwd (originally attributed to initscripts): insecure permissions for /var/log
# Risk: low — not relevant in a container environment
CVE-2007-5686

# glibc: glob implementation excessive CPU/memory with crafted expressions
# Risk: low — not reachable from MCP API surface
CVE-2010-4756

# apt/libapt-pkg7.0 (originally attributed to apt-key): does not validate signatures correctly
# Risk: low — apt is a build-time tool, not invoked in the production stage
CVE-2011-3374

# perl: File::Temp insecure temporary file handling
# Risk: low — perl not used by this application at runtime
CVE-2011-4116

# systemd (libsystemd0/libudev1): TOCTOU race condition updating file permissions and SELinux contexts
# Risk: low — systemd not used inside this container
CVE-2013-4392

# coreutils: race condition in chown/chgrp
# Risk: low — coreutils not invoked by the MCP server at runtime
CVE-2017-18018

# glibc: uncontrolled recursion in check_dst_limits_calc_pos_1 (regex)
# Risk: low — not reachable from MCP API surface
CVE-2018-20796

# glibc: stack guard protection bypass
# Risk: low — container runs as non-root; not exploitable from MCP API surface
CVE-2019-1010022

# glibc: running ldd on malicious ELF leads to code execution
# Risk: low — ldd not invoked at runtime; no untrusted ELF loading
CVE-2019-1010023

# glibc: ASLR bypass using thread stack/heap cache
# Risk: low — not reachable from MCP API surface
CVE-2019-1010024

# glibc: heap address disclosure via pthread
# Risk: low — not reachable from MCP API surface
CVE-2019-1010025

# glibc: uncontrolled recursion in check_dst_limits_calc_pos_1 (regex)
# Risk: low — not reachable from MCP API surface
CVE-2019-9192

# sqlite: crafted SQL query allows sensitive information disclosure
# Risk: low — sqlite3 is a Python stdlib dependency; MCP API does not accept raw SQL
CVE-2021-45346

# util-linux family (bsdutils, libblkid1, liblastlog2-2, libmount1, libsmartcols1,
# libuuid1, login, mount): partial disclosure of arbitrary files in chfn/chsh with libreadline
# Risk: low — chfn/chsh are not invoked by this application
CVE-2022-0563

# systemd: attacker can modify sealed log file
# Risk: low — systemd not used inside this container
CVE-2023-31437

# systemd: attacker can truncate sealed log file
# Risk: low — systemd not used inside this container
CVE-2023-31438

# systemd: attacker can modify sealed log contents
# Risk: low — systemd not used inside this container
CVE-2023-31439

# login.defs/passwd (originally attributed to shadow-utils): default subordinate ID config could lead to compromise
# Risk: low — container runs as non-root; subordinate IDs not configured
CVE-2024-56433

# coreutils: heap buffer under-read in sort via key specification
# Risk: low — coreutils not invoked by the MCP server at runtime
CVE-2025-5278

# gnu-ncurses (libncursesw6, libtinfo6, ncurses-base, ncurses-bin): stack buffer overflow
# Risk: low — ncurses is a system library; not reachable from MCP API surface
CVE-2025-6141

# tar: rmt command may have undesired side effects (TEMP ID)
# Risk: low — tar not invoked by this application at runtime
TEMP-0290435-0B57B5

# sysvinit-utils: no-root option in expert installer (TEMP ID)
# Risk: low — sysvinit not relevant in a container environment
TEMP-0517018-A83CE6

# login.defs/passwd (originally attributed to shadow): privilege escalation related to CVE-2005-4890 (TEMP ID)
# Risk: low — container runs as non-root; not exploitable from MCP API surface
TEMP-0628843-DBAD28

# bash (originally attributed to shadow): privilege escalation to other users (TEMP ID)
# Risk: low — container runs as non-root; not exploitable from MCP API surface
TEMP-0841856-B18BAF
